{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Therefore the name of the city is Be'er Sheva.</b> And if you ask: it has been called Be'er Sheva since the days of Abraham! Rather, this is what it says: <b>and he called it</b> the well <b>Sheva, because of</b> the fact that the name of the city was already called Be'er Sheva. However, initially it was called Be'er Sheva on account of the oath, and through that they now came there to renew the oath. One may ask: how did Isaac form a partnership with Avimelekh, when we say in tractate Avodah Zarah that it contains the matter of 'before the blind you shall not place a stumbling block' — for he transgressed 'let it be heard through your mouth'?"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:09.911551229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}